{
  "version": 2,
  "builds": [
    {
      "src": "app.py",
      "use": "@vercel/python"
    }
  ],
  "routes": [
    {
      "src": "/(.*)",
      "dest": "app.py"
    }
  ]
}



### Step 2: Add `wsgi.py` (To help Vercel find Flask)
Sometimes Vercel looks for a standard WSGI file to wrap Flask apps. Create a new file in your root folder named **`wsgi.py`** and put this inside:

```python
from app import app

if __name__ == "__main__":
    app.run()